# Permanents that leave the battlefield together are all judged against the battlefield as it was before (CR 614.12, 101.4):
# Dauthi Voidwalker, destroyed by Bot2's Wrath of God together with Bot2's Ornithopter (which came after it), is still there for
# the Ornithopter's move, so the Ornithopter is exiled (with a void counter) instead of put into Bot2's graveyard. Bot2's Black
# Lotus, sacrificed for the Wrath while the Voidwalker was there, is exiled too. The Voidwalker itself goes to its owner's
# graveyard (it only touches an opponent's), and Wrath of God, finishing its resolution after the Voidwalker has left, goes to
# Bot2's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Dauthi Voidwalker
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Wrath of God
Island x20

